      "name": "IMCCE / SE-OP (Observatoire de Paris) \u2014 Miriade rise/transit/set service",
      "url_template": "https://ssp.imcce.fr/webservices/miriade/api/rts.php?-body=11&-observer={lon}%20{lat}%20{elevation_m}&-ep={date}&-nbd=1&-tz=0&-twilight=1&-fmt=time:second&-mime=json",
      "resolution": "1 second, truncated (SSC's values run ~0.9 s late against it, consistently, which is the truncation and not an error)",
      "convention": "Twilights are the geometric centre of the Sun at -6, -12 and -18 deg with no refraction and no semidiameter. transit-sup is the upper meridian transit. Body id 11 is the Sun.",
