  "outcome_rules": [
    "occurs: the almanac printed a time.",
    "always_above / always_below: the almanac said so explicitly ('Object continuously above/below the Horizon' / 'the Twilight Limit'), or \u2014 for a twilight \u2014 the Sun rose and set that day yet the deeper twilight is absent, which can only mean it never reached that depression.",
    "not_in_window: USNO printed neither a time nor a continuously-above/below note, so the phenomenon simply fell outside that UTC day (the Moon's 24h50m cycle)."
